* {{audio|De-Bauer.ogg|audio|lang=de}}
* {{rhymes|aʊ̯ɐ|lang=de}}

===Etymology 1===
From {{etyl|gmh|de}} {{term|būre|lang=gmh}}, {{term|gebūre|lang=gmh}}, from {{etyl|goh|de}} {{term|būr|lang=goh}}, {{term|gibūr|lang=goh}}, {{term|gibūro|lang=goh}}, from {{etyl|gem-pro|de}} {{m|gem-pro|*būraz}}. Compare English {{term|bower|lang=en}}, {{term|boor|lang=en}}, Dutch {{term|boer|lang=nl}}, {{term|buur|lang=nl}}.

====Noun====
{{de-noun|m|Bauern|Bauern}}

# [[farmer]], [[peasant]], [[boor]]
# {{context|chess|lang=de}} [[pawn]]

=====Usage notes=====
* ''Bauer'' is a weak noun in the standard language, but is part of a group of nouns which have a stark tendency to be strong colloquially, so one will often hear ''dem Bauer'' instead of ''dem Bauern''.

